n,", "x0": 0.12967032967032968, "y0": 0.3815073815073815, "x1": 0.2571428571428571, "y1": 0.3962703962703963}, {"text": "13. The table below shows the threshold frequencies for five different metallic elements.", "x0": 0.046153846153846156, "y0": 0.43045843045843046, "x1": 0.7736263736263737, "y1": 0.445998445998446}, {"text": "Metal Threshold Frequency Bz", "x0": 0.24945054945054945, "y0": 0.4763014763014763, "x1": 0.7505494505494505, "y1": 0.5019425019425019}, {"text": "\u2018Aluminium 99", "x0": 0.24395604395604395, "y0": 0.5019425019425019, "x1": 0.5, "y1": 0.5275835275835276}, {"text": "Magnesium 8.7 -", "x0": 0.24285714285714285, "y0": 0.5314685314685315, "x1": 0.9175824175824175, "y1": 0.5516705516705517}, {"text": "Zine TA", "x0": 0.24615384615384617, "y0": 0.5532245532245532, "x1": 0.4989010989010989, "y1": 0.5788655788655789}, {"text": "Sodium 35", "x0": 0.24615384615384617, "y0": 0.5788655788655789, "x1": 0.4978021978021978, "y1": 0.6045066045066045}, {"text": "Caesium 4.4", "x0": 0.24505494505494504, "y0": 0.6091686091686092, "x1": 0.4978021978021978, "y1": 0.6301476301476302}, {"text": "From which of these metals will electrons be emitted if each is lit by'light of 7.2 x 10\" Hz,", "x0": 0.06923076923076923, "y0": 0.6464646464646465, "x1": 0.9098901098901099, "y1": 0.6721056721056721}, {"text": "(@) Aluminium, Magnesium and Zine.", "x0": 0.06923076923076923, "y0": 0.6884226884226884, "x1": 0.4032967032967033, "y1": 0.703962703962704}, {"text": "(b) Caesium and Sodium", "x0": 0.06813186813186813, "y0": 0.7055167055167055, "x1": 0.2934065934065934, "y1": 0.7202797202797203}, {"text": "(c) All of the metallic elements", "x0": 0.06703296703296703, "y0": 0.7218337218337219, "x1": 0.34505494505494505, "y1": 0.7373737373737373}, {"text": "(d) None of the metallic elements", "x0": 0.06703296703296703, "y0": 0.7389277389277389, "x1": 0.3637362637362637, "y1": 0.7544677544677545}, {"text": "14. The drift velocity of electrons in a conductor is related to the", "x