r answers on this sheet", "x0": 0.054945054945054944, "y0": 0.14296814296814297, "x1": 0.3934065934065934, "y1": 0.16317016317016317}, {"text": "16. A 100 kg man has a weight of 1 on the planet Krypton. Calculate the acceleration of gravity", "x0": 0.05714285714285714, "y0": 0.1888111888111888, "x1": 0.9076923076923077, "y1": 0.2128982128982129}, {"text": "on Krypton. 1", "x0": 0.0978021978021978, "y0": 0.20590520590520592, "x1": 0.9274725274725275, "y1": 0.22999222999222999}, {"text": "17. a) Describe Galileo\u2019s analysis of projectile motion,", "x0": 0.05824175824175824, "y0": 0.32867132867132864, "x1": 0.5252747252747253, "y1": 0.34965034965034963}, {"text": "b) The diagram below isa record of a stroboscopic photograph of the motion of a projectile fired", "x0": 0.0978021978021978, "y0": 0.4592074592074592, "x1": 0.9010989010989011, "y1": 0.48329448329448327}, {"text": "horizontal surface. The time interval between images is 0.5 seconds, Take the acceleration", "x0": 0.15714285714285714, "y0": 0.47241647241647244, "x1": 0.8989010989010989, "y1": 0.4965034965034965}, {"text": "due to gravity (g) as 10 ms\u201d,", "x0": 0.0978021978021978, "y0": 0.49572649572649574, "x1": 0.33296703296703295, "y1": 0.515928515928516}, {"text": "HORIZONTAL DISTANCE {1m}", "x0": 0.4472527472527473, "y0": 0.728049728049728, "x1": 0.6615384615384615, "y1": 0.7498057498057498}, {"text": "\u2018When the horizontal distance travelled by the projectile is 18m, the vertical component of its velocity", "x0": 0.08351648351648351, "y0": 0.7474747474747475, "x1": 0.9208791208791208, "y1": 0.7762237762237763}, {"text": "is zero.", "x0": 0.08351648351648351, "y0": 0.7816627816627817, "x1": 0.14175824175824175, "y1": 0.7933177933177933}, {"text": "() What is the range of the projectile?", "x0": 0.0945054945054945, "y0": 0.811965811965812, "x1": 0.41208791208791207, "y1": 0.8306138306138307}, {"text": "(ii) What is the time of flight of the projectile?", "x0": 0.09340659340659341, "y0": 0.8772338772338772, "x1": 0.4758241758241758, "y1": 0.8997668997668997}, {"text": "this question continued over page:", "x0": 0.6164835164835165, "y0": 0.9611499611499611, "x1": 0.9032967032967033, "y1": 0.9712509712509713}], [{"text": "(iv) What was the vertical component of its initial velocity? 2", "x0": 0.11208791208791209, "y0": 0.08391608391608392, "x1": 0.9395604395604396, "y1": 0.1048951048951049}, {"text": "19, Describe two difficulties associated with effective and reliable communications between satellites", "x0": 0.07032967032967033, "y0": 0.3838383838383838, "x1": 0.9120879120879121, "y1": 0.4017094017094017}, {"text": "and Earth, 3", "x0": 0.11208791208791209, "y0": 0.40093240093240096, "x1": 0.9395604395604396, "y1": 0.4172494172494173}, {"text": "20. Describe an investigation that you carried out in class, which demonstrates the changes in the motion.", "x0": 0.06593406593406594, "y0": 0.5827505827505828, "x1": 0.9384615384615385, "y1": 0.6021756021756022}, {"text": "of a Satellite as it approaches the parent body. Relate this to the motion of areal satellite. 3", "x0": 0.1076923076923077, "y0": 0.5998445998445998, "x1": 0.9395604395604396, "y1": 0.6192696192696193}], [{"text": "21, A spaceship of length 20m flies a", "x0": 0.04395604395604396, "y0": 0.003108003108003108, "x1": 0.35934065934065934, "y1": 0.03418803418803419}, {"text": "(a) What is the apparent length of \u2018the ee from the observer on Earth? 1", "x0": 0.08681318681318681, "y0": 0.028749028749028748, "x1": 0.9142857142857143, "y1": 0.06526806526806526}, {"text": "(b) At what speed would a radio transmission from the Earth pass the spacecraft? Explain your", "x0": 0.08791208791208792, "y0": 0.14374514374514374, "x1": 0.8670329670329671, "y1": 0.16627816627816627}, {"text": "answer.", "x0": 0.11868131868131868, "y0": 0.17094017094017094, "x1": 0.1813186813186813, "y1": 0.1794871794871795}, {"text": "22. Below is a diagram of a simple electric motor.", "x0": 0.04395604395604396, "y0": 0.317016